\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
For the uniform sphere of radius sqrt(N), iid standard Gaussian constraint rows $M=floor(\alpha $ N), every $\alpha ,\beta >0$ and bounded continuous real activation phi, does the normalized log partition function converge in mean and probability to $inf_m$ \{alpha $V_(\beta $ phi)(m)+S(m)\} over the stated monotone trial functions, allowing all finite-entropy trials without requiring $m=1$ near the endpoint?

\subsection{Short English statement}
For the uniform sphere of radius sqrt(N), iid standard Gaussian constraint rows $M=floor(\alpha $ N), every $\alpha ,\beta >0$ and bounded continuous real activation phi, does the normalized log partition function converge in mean and probability to $inf_m$ \{alpha $V_(\beta $ phi)(m)+S(m)\} over the stated monotone trial functions, allowing all finite-entropy trials without requiring $m=1$ near the endpoint?

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] Original question source or mathematical context.
\url{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/The-free-energy-of-the-spherical-random-perceptron-September-24-2026/build/paper.tex}.
